{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-18372" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $c=⟨-2,0,0⟩$ and $d=⟨4,-1,0⟩.$ Find the scalar projection of $c$ onto $d.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca410b5b6acd13fe8f0d6c25e8de15241e0aedd1d05c4ac09c3efeedad2601d"} {"question" "q-18372" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{d}\\,c & =\\frac{c\\cdot d}{|\\,d\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{c}_{x}{d}_{x}+{c}_{y}{d}_{y}+{c}_{z}{d}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{d}_{x}^{2}+{d}_{y}^{2}+{d}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2\\cdot 4+0\\cdot (-1)+0\\cdot 0}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{17}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca410b5b6acd13fe8f0d6c25e8de15241e0aedd1d05c4ac09c3efeedad2601d"} {"question" "q-18372" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8122f22a30d313865c55646d63ce92feeeacacacc47abc01b1aeb0480b235ffe"} {"question" "q-18372" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca410b5b6acd13fe8f0d6c25e8de15241e0aedd1d05c4ac09c3efeedad2601d"} {"question" "q-18372" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "-\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{17}}"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "\\sqrt{17}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca410b5b6acd13fe8f0d6c25e8de15241e0aedd1d05c4ac09c3efeedad2601d"} {"question" "q-18372" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{17}}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca410b5b6acd13fe8f0d6c25e8de15241e0aedd1d05c4ac09c3efeedad2601d"} {"question" "q-19139" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨3,2,1⟩$ and $b=⟨3,4,1⟩.$ Find the scalar projection of $a$ onto $b.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca410b5b6acd13fe8f0d6c25e8de15241e0aedd1d05c4ac09c3efeedad2601d"} {"question" "q-19139" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 4+1\\cdot 1}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{\\sqrt{26}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca410b5b6acd13fe8f0d6c25e8de15241e0aedd1d05c4ac09c3efeedad2601d"} {"question" "q-19139" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8122f22a30d313865c55646d63ce92feeeacacacc47abc01b1aeb0480b235ffe"} {"question" "q-19139" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca410b5b6acd13fe8f0d6c25e8de15241e0aedd1d05c4ac09c3efeedad2601d"} {"question" "q-19139" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{26}}"] ["math" "\\frac{18}{\\sqrt{14}}"] ["math" "\\frac{18}{\\sqrt{26}}"] ["math" "\\frac{19}{\\sqrt{14}}"] ["math" "\\frac{19}{\\sqrt{26}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca410b5b6acd13fe8f0d6c25e8de15241e0aedd1d05c4ac09c3efeedad2601d"} {"question" "q-19139" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{18}{\\sqrt{26}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca410b5b6acd13fe8f0d6c25e8de15241e0aedd1d05c4ac09c3efeedad2601d"} {"question" "q-236734" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $p=⟨-1,1,2⟩$ and $q=⟨4,x,1⟩.$ Given that the scalar projection of $p$ onto $q$ is zero, find the value of $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca410b5b6acd13fe8f0d6c25e8de15241e0aedd1d05c4ac09c3efeedad2601d"} {"question" "q-236734" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $p$ is a nonzero vector, its scalar projection onto another nonzero vector $q$ equals zero only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\np⊥q\\,⟹\\,p\\cdot q=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & ={p}_{x}\\cdot {q}_{x}+{p}_{y}\\cdot {q}_{y}+{p}_{z}\\cdot {q}_{z} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 4+1\\cdot x+2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =x-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & =0 \\\\ x-2 & =0 \\\\ x & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca410b5b6acd13fe8f0d6c25e8de15241e0aedd1d05c4ac09c3efeedad2601d"} {"question" "q-236734" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8122f22a30d313865c55646d63ce92feeeacacacc47abc01b1aeb0480b235ffe"} {"question" "q-236734" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca410b5b6acd13fe8f0d6c25e8de15241e0aedd1d05c4ac09c3efeedad2601d"} {"question" "q-236734" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca410b5b6acd13fe8f0d6c25e8de15241e0aedd1d05c4ac09c3efeedad2601d"} {"question" "q-236734" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca410b5b6acd13fe8f0d6c25e8de15241e0aedd1d05c4ac09c3efeedad2601d"} {"question" "q-236735" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $p=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ and $q=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].$ Given that the scalar projection of $p$ onto $q$ is $0,$ find the value of $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca410b5b6acd13fe8f0d6c25e8de15241e0aedd1d05c4ac09c3efeedad2601d"} {"question" "q-236735" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $p$ is a nonzero vector, its scalar projection onto another nonzero vector $q$ equals zero only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\np⊥q\\,⟹\\,p\\cdot q=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & ={p}_{x}\\cdot {q}_{x}+{p}_{y}\\cdot {q}_{y}+{p}_{z}\\cdot {q}_{z} \\\\  & =6\\cdot x+1\\cdot 4+4\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =6x-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & =0 \\\\ 6x-12 & =0 \\\\ 6x & =12 \\\\ x & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca410b5b6acd13fe8f0d6c25e8de15241e0aedd1d05c4ac09c3efeedad2601d"} {"question" "q-236735" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8122f22a30d313865c55646d63ce92feeeacacacc47abc01b1aeb0480b235ffe"} {"question" "q-236735" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca410b5b6acd13fe8f0d6c25e8de15241e0aedd1d05c4ac09c3efeedad2601d"} {"question" "q-236735" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca410b5b6acd13fe8f0d6c25e8de15241e0aedd1d05c4ac09c3efeedad2601d"} {"question" "q-236735" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca410b5b6acd13fe8f0d6c25e8de15241e0aedd1d05c4ac09c3efeedad2601d"} {"question" "q-319254" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $p=3i+2j-k$ and $q=-2i+xj.$ Given that the scalar projection of $p$ onto $q$ is zero, find the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca410b5b6acd13fe8f0d6c25e8de15241e0aedd1d05c4ac09c3efeedad2601d"} {"question" "q-319254" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $p$ is a nonzero vector, its scalar projection onto another nonzero vector $q$ equals zero only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\np⊥q\\,⟹\\,p\\cdot q=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & ={p}_{x}\\cdot {q}_{x}+{p}_{y}\\cdot {q}_{y}+{p}_{z}\\cdot {q}_{z} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-2)+2\\cdot x+(-1)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =-6+2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & =0 \\\\ -6+2x & =0 \\\\ 2x & =6 \\\\ x & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ca410b5b6acd13fe8f0d6c25e8de15241e0aedd1d05c4ac09c3efeedad2601d"} {"question" "q-319254" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003439/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8122f22a30d313865c55646d63ce92feeeacacacc47abc01b1aeb0480b235ffe"} {"question" "q-319254" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/matha